# Build, verification, and extraction

## Build & Verification Front Door

Plain `cargo` is the build front door. `scripts/check-workspace.sh` is the only
repository-wide verification front door. It owns formatting, ShellCheck,
resolved workspace-graph and safety policy, Python and extraction contracts,
Semgrep regression guards, the Cargo feature matrix, workspace tests, isolated
feature capability tests, documented selector validation, generated-guidance
drift, and dependency policy.

Semgrep contracts execute the actual engine against repository-shaped rejecting
and permitted fixtures for every rule. Missing rule fixtures, skipped source
files, parse errors and timeouts fail closed. Per-rule scan timeout is 30 seconds;
this accommodates large owner files without accepting incomplete scans.

```bash
scripts/check-workspace.sh
```

For a shorter local check of the in-memory feature set, run
`scripts/check-workspace.sh --in-memory`. It runs the same static and contract
checks, then checks that the selected dependency graph contains no Redb, runs
workspace Clippy and tests with `core/full`, `facade/full`, and `testkit/full`,
and executes eight in-memory/fixture feature capability selectors. It does not
run the per-feature Clippy matrix, Redb-backed tests, or documented selector
validation. Its success is explicitly scoped and is not extraction or full
workspace qualification.

Run focused commands while developing, but do not report them as equivalent to
the canonical rail. The feature matrix discovers feature names from Cargo
metadata and covers default, bare, every feature other than the `default`/`full`
aliases, explicit `full`, and workspace all-features; adding a manifest feature
therefore adds it to the matrix without editing a shell list.

Examples use the real public APIs:

```bash
cargo run -p quanta-memory-platform-facade --example hello_world
cargo run -p quanta-memory-platform-facade --example effective_budget_report
```

Generated guidance:

```bash
python3 tools/pm/pm.py sync
python3 tools/pm/pm.py lint
python3 tools/pm/pm.py status
python3 -m unittest -q tools/pm/tests/test_pm.py
```

The prompt manager is Python-standard-library-only. Its JSON manifest rejects
orphan sources, duplicate and unknown keys, orphaned generated outputs,
path escapes, missing outputs, and drift. The workspace-policy parser uses
Python 3.11+ `tomllib` or `tomli` on older Python; a missing parser fails the gate.
The full and in-memory gates reject ignored Rust tests and skipped or expected-failure Python contracts. Live CircleCI trigger
binding is a separate external check: `python3 scripts/verify-hosted-ci-binding.py`.
The Rust toolchain version is owned solely by `rust-toolchain.toml`; dependency
policy is owned by `deny.toml`; formatting is owned by `rustfmt.toml`. Workspace
Rust/Clippy lint levels are owned by the root `Cargo.toml`; each library root
also retains `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` so a local `allow` cannot weaken the
portable-library boundary.

Extraction is mechanical and fail-closed:

```bash
scripts/extract-to-standalone-repo.sh --dry-run /path/to/dest   # pre-flight only
scripts/extract-to-standalone-repo.sh /path/to/dest             # copy + verify + commit
```
